# Documentation index (`[permanent project knowledge dir]`)

`[dir]` answers **"how does the software work?"** — permanent, authoritative, committed
knowledge for humans and agents. Process knowledge (how anyone should *work* here) lives in
`[permanent process knowledge dir]` instead.

| Path | Answers |
| --- | --- |
| `[guide/]` | How to use it — for the person actually using the finished system. |
| `[spec path]` | What we are building — the authoritative spec; do not deviate without recording why. |
| `[architecture/]` | How the pieces fit together: boundaries, data model, test strategy. |
| `[api/ or interfaces/]` | Request/response or interface contracts. |
| `[development/]` | How to run, build, test, and debug locally. |
| `[operations/]` | Provisioning, release, observability/rollback approach, the manual
verification checklist, the runbook. |
| `[design/]` | The design system and accessibility standard, if this project has a designer
function — otherwise omit this row. |
| `[security/]` | This project's own security facts: what data it handles, its trust boundaries,
its auth model, anything a contributor must know before touching a sensitive surface. Distinct
from `principles/08`'s universal build/operate rules, which live in process knowledge, not here. |
| `[adr/]` | The decision log — see `templates/adr-template.md`. |

